! jb_ax5b "I-Box 5", routine 1260 TEST 7 continued -- "CHK LOWER
! BOUNDARY DATA." and "CHK BOUNDARY CONTROL BIT."  PDF p.68 (printed
! p.65), octal 022264.40-022306.40, transcribed VERBATIM at the
! listing's own addresses, checked bit-exactly by
! verify_ax5b_160102_listing.py AND RUN ON THE MODEL.
!
! The upper-boundary half is ax5b_16099_ub_data.strap (p.65).  This is
! the rest of TEST 7: the other register, and the control bit.
!
! THE LOWER-BOUNDARY LOOP (I60102/I60103) MIRRORS THE UPPER ONE
! exactly -- eighteen iterations, because the lower boundary is word 3
! bits 32-49 -- with three differences worth naming: it stores through
! $LB rather than $UB, it indexes its error table with $X2 rather than
! $X3, and that table is I60B18 at 022313.40, whose entries pp.69-70
! print as "LOWER BOUNDARY DATA FAILURE, BIT 32" upward.
!
! THE CONTROL-BIT TEST is the interesting half.  Word 3 bit 57 is the
! boundary control bit (Ref. Manual p.31: it "determines which
! condition will cause an address monitoring signal").  The deck sets
! it from BIT57, reads word 3 back, moves the refill field with
! "SR,$X1,$X1", and compares against BIT11 -- bit 57 sits at refill
! position 57-46 = 11.  Then it clears word 3 with "Z,$UB" and
! compares against I00Z, the zero index word.  Two error messages:
! "-UNABLE TO SET BNDRY CNTRL TO 1." and "...TO 0."
!
! A FOURTH CONFIRMATION OF THE BIT TABLE.  This page names BIT57 and
! BIT11; they print as 24613 and 24535, and 024522 + 57 = 024613,
! 024522 + 11 = 024535.  The rule read off p.114 holds at 0, 11, 17,
! 18 and 57.  I00Z prints as 24502, matching p.114's "ZERO INDX WD."
!
! WHY IT RUNS DISABLED: word 3 is permanently protected (p.31), so an
! enabled store into it raises DS and is suppressed.  Disabled is the
! reset state and this block never enables.
!
! SUBSTITUTIONS: three, the same shape as the p.65 block.
!   1. None in the deck's own label names.  This item used to read
!      "numeric labels prefixed L": the leading glyph of I60102,
!      I60103, I60104, I60B18 and I00Z was read as a digit and an "L"
!      prefixed to make each legal for this assembler.  Measured, it
!      is the letter I (docs/listing_typography.md), so the names are
!      written as the page prints them and nothing is prefixed.  The
!      L0..L17 labels below are NOT survivors of that: they are this
!      transcription's own names for the eighteen hangs in item 2,
!      invented here, and the run has an L0 and an L2..L9 that no
!      digit reading could ever have produced.
!   2. I60B18's eighteen entries are "B,$" hangs at the deck's own
!      three-half-word spacing, so a failure on bit N halts at
!      I60B18 + N*1.32 and the address NAMES THE BIT.  The deck's real
!      entries end "BD,I60104" -- it REPORTS AND CONTINUES, testing all
!      eighteen; these hangs stop at the first.  SERS is a hang too.
!   3. A "BEW,$" exit at 022307.00, where the listing continues with
!      "B,$+1.0".
! BIT0..BIT17, BIT57 and I00Z are derived from p.114's stated rule
! rather than transcribed row by row.

BIT0    SYN, (8)24522.0
BIT11   SYN, (8)24535.0
BIT57   SYN, (8)24613.0
I00Z   SYN, (8)24502.0
I60B18 SYN, (8)22313.40
SEN     SYN, (8)1310.0
SERS    SYN, (8)1304.0

        SLC, (8)22264.40
I60102 LVI, $X1, 0.0              ! -CHK LOWER BOUNDARY DATA.
        LCI, $X1, 18
        LVI, $X2, 0.0
I60103 Z,   $MASK
        LV,  $X3, BIT0($X1)
        SV,  $X3, $LB              !  word 3 bits 32-49
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        LV,  $X3, $LB
        KV,  $X3, BIT0($X1)
        BXE, $+1.0
        B,   I60B18($X2)          ! -DATA ERROR.
I60104 V+I, $X2, 1.32
        CB+, $X1, I60103
!
        LX,  $X1, BIT57            ! -CHK BOUNDARY CONTROL BIT.
        SX,  $X1, $UB
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        LX,  $X1, $UB
        SR,  $X1, $X1
        KV,  $X1, BIT11            !  bit 57 is refill position 11
        SIC, SEN
        BZXE, SERS                 ! -UNABLE TO SET BNDRY CNTRL TO 1.
!
        Z,   $UB
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        LX,  $X1, $UB
        SR,  $X1, $X1
        KV,  $X1, I00Z
        SIC, SEN
        BZXE, SERS                 ! -UNABLE TO SET BNDRY CNTRL TO 0.
!
        SLC, (8)22307.0
PASS    BEW, $
!
        SLC, (8)1304.0
SERSH   B, $
        SLC, (8)1310.0
SENW    DD(BU,64), 0
!
        SLC, (8)22313.40
L0      B, $                       ! LOWER BOUNDARY DATA FAILURE, BIT 32
        SLC, (8)22315.0
L1      B, $                       ! LOWER BOUNDARY DATA FAILURE, BIT 33
        SLC, (8)22316.40
L2      B, $                       ! LOWER BOUNDARY DATA FAILURE, BIT 34
        SLC, (8)22320.0
L3      B, $                       ! LOWER BOUNDARY DATA FAILURE, BIT 35
        SLC, (8)22321.40
L4      B, $                       ! LOWER BOUNDARY DATA FAILURE, BIT 36
        SLC, (8)22323.0
L5      B, $                       ! LOWER BOUNDARY DATA FAILURE, BIT 37
        SLC, (8)22324.40
L6      B, $                       ! LOWER BOUNDARY DATA FAILURE, BIT 38
        SLC, (8)22326.0
L7      B, $                       ! LOWER BOUNDARY DATA FAILURE, BIT 39
        SLC, (8)22327.40
L8      B, $                       ! LOWER BOUNDARY DATA FAILURE, BIT 40
        SLC, (8)22331.0
L9      B, $                       ! LOWER BOUNDARY DATA FAILURE, BIT 41
        SLC, (8)22332.40
L10     B, $                       ! LOWER BOUNDARY DATA FAILURE, BIT 42
        SLC, (8)22334.0
L11     B, $                       ! LOWER BOUNDARY DATA FAILURE, BIT 43
        SLC, (8)22335.40
L12     B, $                       ! LOWER BOUNDARY DATA FAILURE, BIT 44
        SLC, (8)22337.0
L13     B, $                       ! LOWER BOUNDARY DATA FAILURE, BIT 45
        SLC, (8)22340.40
L14     B, $                       ! LOWER BOUNDARY DATA FAILURE, BIT 46
        SLC, (8)22342.0
L15     B, $                       ! LOWER BOUNDARY DATA FAILURE, BIT 47
        SLC, (8)22343.40
L16     B, $                       ! LOWER BOUNDARY DATA FAILURE, BIT 48
        SLC, (8)22345.0
L17     B, $                       ! LOWER BOUNDARY DATA FAILURE, BIT 49
!
        SLC, (8)24502.0
Z100    DD(BU,64), 0               ! I00Z, "ZERO INDX WD."
        SLC, (8)24522.0
B0      DD(BU,64), 9223372036854775808  ! BIT0
B1      DD(BU,64), 4611686018427387904  ! BIT1
B2      DD(BU,64), 2305843009213693952  ! BIT2
B3      DD(BU,64), 1152921504606846976  ! BIT3
B4      DD(BU,64), 576460752303423488  ! BIT4
B5      DD(BU,64), 288230376151711744  ! BIT5
B6      DD(BU,64), 144115188075855872  ! BIT6
B7      DD(BU,64), 72057594037927936  ! BIT7
B8      DD(BU,64), 36028797018963968  ! BIT8
B9      DD(BU,64), 18014398509481984  ! BIT9
B10     DD(BU,64), 9007199254740992  ! BIT10
B11     DD(BU,64), 4503599627370496  ! BIT11
B12     DD(BU,64), 2251799813685248  ! BIT12
B13     DD(BU,64), 1125899906842624  ! BIT13
B14     DD(BU,64), 562949953421312  ! BIT14
B15     DD(BU,64), 281474976710656  ! BIT15
B16     DD(BU,64), 140737488355328  ! BIT16
B17     DD(BU,64), 70368744177664  ! BIT17
        SLC, (8)24613.0
B57     DD(BU,64), 64  ! BIT57
        END, I60102
